    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Our experimental paradigm relies on lipofection of a self-inactivating, integrative lentiviral vector expressing the chimeric Cas9 nuclease paired with a single-guide RNA complementary to the 5' end of exon 1 of the *PCSK9* gene promotor to facilitate efficient nucleoprotein complex formation. This precise molecular targeting induces a double-strand break, triggering NHEJ-mediated indel generation that results in frameshift mutations and functional ablation of the apoptotic particle assembly machinery. Subsequent validation involves spike-in normalized single-cell 10x Genomics sequencing to quantify allele-specific discontinuities and rule out ectopic cleavage events within the PRDM10 or *APOE* loci. Finally, longitudinal pharmacokinetic profiling utilizing quantitative Mass Spectrometry-enabled ELISAs will measure the hemodynamic clearance of isoform-19b PCSK9 and the corresponding reduction in systemic LDL-cholesterol esterified complexes. This high-fidelity, multi-modal stratification ensures strict adherence to orthogonality criteria for next-generation gene therapeutic interventions.",
